<title>UK: DUTCH TAXES THWART ANY SHELL SHARE BUY-BACK.</title>
<headline>DUTCH TAXES THWART ANY SHELL SHARE BUY-BACK.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell said on Thursday the stringent Dutch tax regime would make a share buy-back for the Anglo-Dutch oil giant not worth its while.</p>
<p>&quot;In the Netherlands it is impractical,&quot; said Shell Transport and Trading chairman Mark Moody-Stuart.</p>
<p>&quot;But that may change,&quot; he said, adding Shell was in talks with the Dutch fiscal authorities about the share buy-back issue.</p>
<p>Shell Transport and Trading owns 40 percent of the Royal Dutch/Shell Group. Royal Dutch Petroleum owns the remainder.</p>
<p>Royal Dutch may look into any share buy-back once the Dutch tax regime changes, Moody-Stuart said, adding that Shell Transport and Trading continues to consider the matter in the meantime.</p>
<p>&quot;But we would rather move in parallel,&quot; Moody-Stuart said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
